<title>MOROCCO: French fund lends Morocco $16.7 mln for railway.</title>
<headline>French fund lends Morocco $16.7 mln for railway.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A French fund granted Morocco's state-owned railway utility the equivalent of $16.7 million to buy nine locomotives from GEC-Alsthom, the official MAP news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The loan will be repayable by railway firm Societe Nationale des Chemins de Fer (SNCF) over 15 years with a seven-year grace period, MAP said.</p>
<p>Morocco started in 1996 a long term investment plan to upgrade its railway equipment and 2,000 km network worth 5.2 billion dirhams ($547 million) financed mainly by loans from foreign institutions, including the World Bank.</p>
<p>($1= 9.5 dirhams)</p>
<p>- Rabat newsroom +212-7 72 65 18</p>
</text>
